<title>SINGAPORE: TABLE-SINGAPORE FINANCE HALF YR UP 6.6 PCT.</title>
<headline>TABLE-SINGAPORE FINANCE HALF YR UP 6.6 PCT.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1997</p>
<p>		   (in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			   16.44   vs    15.42</p>
<p>    Group shr (cents)		   9.00   vs    10.55</p>
<p>    Group shr fully diluted (cents) 8.37   vs     9.61</p>
<p>    Operating income		   66.32   vs    69.94</p>
<p>    Investment income		   0.75   vs     0.71</p>
<p>    Interest (expense)		  1.78   vs     3.69</p>
<p>    Depreciation and amortisation   0.66   vs     0.66</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit		     22.38   vs    21.03</p>
<p>    Tax				     5.94   vs     5.61</p>
<p>Note - Full name Singapore Finance Ltd. It said the results were arrived at after making total loan provisions amounting to $3.1 million for the group and the company. It said results for the first half year just ended reflect slack loan demand combined with intensifying competition. The outlook for the year remains uncertain but operations are expected to stay profitable.</p>
